  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d95f71226bf26bc4caed6a0458a3b538, type: 3}
  m_Name: Lesson 8 Question 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: Why don't Christians have to feel God's judgment?
  answers:
  - Because God makes them blameless
  - Really, they should
  - Because God pretends not to see their sins
  - Because it's not scary
  correctAnswerIndex: 0
  discussionAnswer: God by His own power makes Christians righteous. He cleanses
    every believer from sin so that they are blameless at the future day of judgment,
    and He has promised He will never reverse His work of righteousness in a believer's
    life.
